# Attribution

`pi-subagent-herdr` is a derivative work of
[`badlogic/pi-subagent`](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-subagent) by
[badlogic](https://github.com/badlogic).

The following are inherited from that project:

- The command surface: `spawn`, `send`, `wait`, `stop`, `rename`, and `list`,
  including their argument names and semantics.
- The control-inbox message channel (`inbox/*.json`, atomically written, ordered
  by filename), and the `auto` versus `followUp` delivery distinction.
- The two-mode extension structure: one file that serves both the parent UI and,
  when `PI_SUBAGENT_RUN_DIR` is set, the child-side control bridge.
- The launch-manifest idea of storing relaunch parameters and parent session
  ownership, and the atomic write of that record.
- The transcript reader that reconstructs the active branch by walking `parentId`
  back from the newest entry, so compaction and branching cannot return a stale
  assistant message.
- Substantial portions of the prose in `skills/subagent/SKILL.md`, particularly
  the tool-list and isolation-flag explanations.

The following are new in this project:

- The Herdr substrate throughout: tab-per-subagent topology, `herdr.ts`, the
  socket event subscription, and the removal of the tmux lifecycle machinery.
- Token, cost, and tool-count metrics reported through
  `herdr pane report-metadata`.
- `blocked` detection, including the `herdr:blocked` event emitter that Herdr's
  own Pi integration listens for but does not itself provide.
- The launch-manifest model where status, liveness, identity, and the child
  session path all come from Herdr rather than from a state cache.
- The `read`, `focus`, `doctor`, and `prune` commands, and name resolution
  alongside handles.

